          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Although it has less emphasis in advanced mathematics, and although its definition is more complicated than that of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+of+a+sequence"} limit of a sequence
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lim_{x \to c} f(x) = L
          %p
            means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
            is close to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is sufficiently close to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            here is just a dummy variable, so this is really a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ternary+relation"} ternary relation
            between
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Limits of functions could be defined for functions between various mathematical structures, such as subsets of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolas+Bourbaki"} Nicolas Bourbaki
            or the historical definition, first defined by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karl+Weierstrass"} Karl Weierstrass
            in the context of partial functions on the real numbers and later generalized to metric spaces and topological spaces. Bourbaki’s definition is commonly used in the French language, while Weierstrass’s definition is commonly used in the English language. Weierstrass’s definition is also referred to as the
            %em punctured limit
            of a function (“limite épointée” in French), because it uses
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accumulation+points"} accumulation points
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/punctured+neighborhoods"} punctured neighborhoods
            instead of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adherent+points"} adherent points
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neighborhoods"} neighborhoods
          %h3#in_metric_spaces In metric spaces
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X, d_X)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Y, d_Y)
            be
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metric+spaces"} metric spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            be an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adherent+point"} adherent point
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            be an element in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
          %blockquote
            %p
              the
              %strong
                limit of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
                approaching
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              if for all positive real numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
              there exists a positive real number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              such that for all elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_X(x, c) \lt \delta
              implies that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi f
