          %p
            It would be nice to have notation to distinguish the Bourbaki and Weierstrass versions of limit. One way would be to adopt the Bourbaki definition by default and add the restriction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ≠
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \ne c
            to produce the Weierstrass version. Unfortunately, the Weierstrass definition is the default in most of the world, and then there is no slick way to denote the Bourbaki version.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            A function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
