                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            be the set of tagged partitions of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [a,b]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\colon \Gamma \to X
            map a partition to the maximum length of its parts (often called the norm or mesh of the partition), and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon \Gamma \to Y
            map a tagged partition to the Riemann sum of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on it. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+integral"} Riemann integral
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
